{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And of Benjamin he said.</b> It follows after Levi because the trust of Levi was in the Temple, which is in the portion of Benjamin." "<b>Beloved of YHWH.</b> This is Benjamin the beloved. He dwells securely — upon Him, upon the Shekhinah, next to the Shekhinah — like 'and upon him the tribe of Manasseh' (i.e., upon him, next to him)." "<b>Shelters over him.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He — over Benjamin, and delivers him." "<b>And between his shoulders.</b> His borders, like 'unto the shoulder of the sea of Kinneret.' <b>Shall dwell</b> — that is, between the borders of the Holy One, blessed be He, Benjamin dwelled; his inheritance adjoins the Temple. And since all the tribes were partners in the selling of Joseph, and Benjamin was not a partner with them, and all the tribes were born outside the Land while Benjamin was born in the Land of Israel — he merited that the Shekhinah rest in his portion."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:26.287354043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}